    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0360" n="248" xml:id="pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.111/3588</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-15T10:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Joaquin Tinoco has requested me to ask if there is any objection to his going
                    early in April to France via the United States. He says that if there is no
                    objection, he is going to join French Army at the front through the medium of
                    Costa Rican Minister at Paris. Doubt sincerity of his intention to leave, but if
                    he goes, retirement of Tinoco will be easier of accomplishment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
